<title>UK: First Chicago units win Reuters January forex poll.</title>
<headline>First Chicago units win Reuters January forex poll.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>First Chicago in London and Chicago are joint winners of the Reuter foreign exchange poll for January beating 35 other banks and financial institutions from across the globe.</p>
<p>Levels predicted by First Chicago gave them an average divergence from the actual rate of 3.3234 percent.</p>
<p>Second place went to Lehman Brothers, London, with an average divergence rate of 3.5574, followed by Nikko Bank, also in London, in third place with 3.7988.</p>
<p>The average divergence rates of the 35 polled varied between 3.3234 and 6.4873 percent.</p>
<p>The rankings were based on the accuracy of the forecasts against the European closing rates on January 31 of dollar/mark at 1.6366, dollar/yen at 121.30 and sterling/dollar at 1.6030.</p>
<p>The winners were the only two banks to predict the dollar touching the 120 yen level. The following are the top 20 forecasters and their predictions.</p>
